{"id": 22, "ts": 1780578170.5388167, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I\u2019m shifting my provisional recommendation to **Candidate\u202fC**. While I still value Candidate\u202fB\u2019s stress resilience and technical aptitude, Sarah\u2019s note that B \u201ccan be uncooperative\u201d adds a concrete crew\u2011cooperation concern that directly conflicts with the collaborative nature of long\u2011distance cockpit work. Combined with the already\u2011known weak memory for numbers, B now presents two safety\u2011relevant gaps: attention to detail and teamwork.\nCandidate\u202fC, on the other hand, brings a package of strengths that align tightly with our criteria: 100\u202f% reliability, a positive crew atmosphere, the ability to keep calm in a crisis, and rapid, correct decision\u2011making on complex situations. Although Sarah reports communication difficulties and an egocentric style, the same source also highlights his strong crew\u2011atmosphere contribution, suggesting that his interpersonal impact may be manageable with targeted coaching. Moreover, his limited willingness to further education signals a potential development area, but it does not outweigh his proven operational reliability and decision quality.\nGiven the balance of evidence, Candidate\u202fC offers the most robust overall fit for the long\u2011distance pilot role."}
